#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# power_range

#% text
# `power_range(a, b)` gives `a, 10 a, 100 a, ...` up to `b`; `power_range(a, b, r)` uses the ratio `r`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact arguments give exact elements.

#% item
# A ratio below 1 gives a decreasing range.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
power_range(1, 1000)
#% output
#= [1, 10, 100, 1000]

#% cell
power_range(2, 100, 2)
#% output
#= [2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64]

#% cell
power_range(1/2, 1/100, 1/3)
#% output
#= [1/2, 1/6, 1/18, 1/54]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
power_range(0.001, 10)
#% output
#= [0.001, 0.01, 0.1, 1.0, 10.0]

#% cell
power_range(1, 10^6, 100)
#% output
#= [1, 100, 10000, 1000000]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `range`, `nest_list`
